<h1><span lang="EN-US">Scanning over Defined Area</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="101.32%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Sometimes it is necessary to rescan certain part of an object without adding more data outside this area. For example, if you want edges to be more detailed than the flat areas, then you have to capture more points on these features. It is almost impossible to keep point density higher only on the edges – rescanning them usually will increase the points on the neighbouring areas.</font></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">There is functionality in KUBE that helps to avoid this problem. For the first, you have to scan the whole object with minimum amount of data. Then use some of the Shape selections (Polygonal Selection, Freehand (Lasso) Selection, Rectangular Selection, or Elliptic Selection) to select the areas that you want to rescan.</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Object is scanned</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><span lang="EN-US">Areas for rescan are selected: <a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1">shown below</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP164798710" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><span lang="EN-US"><img src="Scanning_Over_Defined_Area_files/image003.jpg" width="467px" height="346px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-US">After applying the selection, a lasso icon will appear from the left side of</span> <span class="Button">Scan</span> <span lang="EN-US">button (located in the arm driven menu.) This icon will stay there even when you are in</span> <span class="Mode">scan</span> <span lang="EN-US">mode to indicate that scanning is over defined area.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify; font-size:10.0pt;"><img src="images/scanning_over_defined.gif" width="211px" height="53px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Enter in</span> <span class="Mode">scan</span> <span lang="EN-US">mode and start scanning. Points will be captured only if they are within the selection. When you finish and are ready to exit this mode, i.e. for to scan everywhere, simply call</span> <span class="Path">Select &gt; None</span> <span lang="EN-US">or press</span> <b><span class="Shortcut">Ctrl + Q</span></b><span lang="EN-US">.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP159745904" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs6">
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs7">
<td class="whs8">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Point density is higher where the selection was.</font></span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify; font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="Scanning_Over_Defined_Area_files/image007.jpg" width="467px" height="346px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
